          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. State whether True or False"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.107,
            0.753,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Lunar eclipse occurs when the Sun comes between the Earth and the Moon."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.146,
            0.726,
            0.167
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Sunrise happens earlier in Gujarat than in Jharkhand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.167,
            0.752,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) In Chennai, the longest day occurs on the summer solstice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.188,
            0.753,
            0.226
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) We should watch the solar eclipse directly with our naked eye."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.227,
            0.752,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) Seasons occur due to the tilt of Earth’s axis of rotation and its spherical shape."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.266,
            0.753,
            0.305
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vi) The Earth’s revolution around the Sun causes day and night."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.306,
            0.753,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Padmashree saw the Orion constellation nearly overhead at 8 pm yesterday. When will she see Orion overhead today?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.348,
            0.753,
            0.407
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Nandhini saw a group of stars rising at midnight on 21 June. When will she see the same group of stars rising at midnight next year?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.409,
            0.753,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Abhay noticed that when it was daytime in India, his uncle who was in the USA was generally sleeping as it was night-time there. What is the reason behind this difference?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.47,
            0.752,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Four friends used the following ways to see the solar eclipse. Who among them was being careless?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.513,
            0.565,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Ravikiran used a solar eclipse goggle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.537,
            0.658,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Jyothi used a mirror to project the Sun’s image."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.56,
            0.617,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Adithya saw the Sun directly with his eyes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.585,
            0.753,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) Aruna attended a programme arranged by a planetarium."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.609,
            0.752,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. Fill in the circles in Fig. 12.18 appropriately with one of the following: Sun, Moon, Earth."
            }
          ]
        },
